from parts/cut-no-badge.replay
# sys-cut, Route 204 North. Without the Forest Badge (the part): the
# "can be cut" message. With it: A on the tree (FieldMoves_CutTree), yes, and the tree is gone. The
# `cut-*` screenshot lines are the browser spec's key beat: the tree drawn before, gone after, and the
# Cut animation (FIELD_EFFECT_CUT) drawn while it plays.
give badge platinum:BADGE_ID_FOREST
until idle
+0 screenshot cut-before
+0 press a
+1 release a
advance text
until yesno
+0 press a
+1 release a
advance text
until idle
+0 assert flag platinum:FLAG_MAP_LOCAL_HIDE_OBSTACLE_1 true
+0 screenshot cut-after
# the path north is open: walk through where the tree stood
+0 press up
until position 181 677
+0 release up
until idle
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_204_NORTH 181 677
